  "summary": "I wrote the portal scene in `src/main.ts`, but I could not see it render and could not fully typecheck it. `@aura3d/engine` does not resolve in this sandbox: the `node_modules/@aura3d` link is broken. The typecheck tool's only error is \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". I wrote the engine calls from the docs and recipes, so API mistakes would not show up until a real build. I did not run `vite build`.\n\n- **Ruin:** the scene is a dusk ruin with a gradient sky, stars, indigo fog, bloom and a vignette. A two-tier stone platform holds a 24-block stone ring with glowing cyan and violet runes and a glowing inner rim. Around it stand nine pillars (some broken) with a lintel, fallen drums, rubble and glowing floor runes.\n- **Vortex:** the disc inside the ring is a custom GLSL surface with swirling cyan and violet spiral arms that flow inward, a bright pulsing core and a bright rim.\n- **Particles:** 240 sparks spiral into the portal and 110 motes rise from the platform and fade out. They are camera-facing glow sprites whose motion is computed in the GPU shader from one time uniform.\n- **Lighting:** three coloured point lights near the portal pulse slowly. They move in and out every frame. The code also calls `setIntensity` if the node handle has it.\n- **Camera sway:** the whole ruin, lights included, is wrapped in one group that yaws slowly (about ±23° over roughly 39 seconds). I did this because I couldn't find a documented way to move the camera. The lights are inside the group so the lighting stays consistent as it turns.\n- **Required state:** `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { portalActive: true, particleCount, time }` is updated every frame. `particleCount` is the number of particles currently visible. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames are drawn.\n\nUnverified guesses to check first if the render looks wrong:\n- The `blending: \"additive\"` option on the particle material.\n- That the engine passes the particle geometry's position and uv values to the shader u",
